ith a shared purpose.</p><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/work/#the-reading-room' ) ); ?>">See The Reading Room<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div><p>For independent libraries, cultural groups, and neighborhood organizations. We help make existing rooms welcoming and adaptable, balancing public use with storage, upkeep, and the people who run the place.</p><ul><li>Conversations with users and organizers</li><li>Access, circulation, and flexible layouts</li><li>Joinery, lighting, and acoustic intent</li><li>Durable finishes and phased improvements</li></ul></div></section></div>
<section class="section wash"><div class="wrap faq-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow">Before we begin</span><h2>A few useful<br>questions.</h2><p class="fine-print">Every project starts with its own circumstances.</p></div><div><details><summary>When should I speak to an architect?</summary><p>As soon as you have a question about a site or an existing building. Early conversations can help define the brief before you commit to a layout, purchase, or construction schedule.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need a finished brief?</summary><p>No. A few photographs, a rough budget range, and a list of what is and is not working are a useful beginning. We would shape a clearer brief together.</p></details><details><summary>How would fees be agreed?</summary><p>After an initial discussion, the scope, stages, deliverables, and exclusions would be set out in a written proposal. Specialist advice and statutory fees would be identified separately; this sample does not quote fees.</p></details><details><summary>Can the work happen in stages?</summary><p>Yes, when the building and scope allow it. We would plan the whole first, then consider sensible phases so that early work does not prevent later improvements.</p></details><details><summary>Are these completed projects?</summary><p>No. Common Ground and the three portfolio projects are fictional. Photographs are approved architectural references, not images of built work by this practice.</p></details></div></div></section><?php get_template_part( 'template-parts/inquiry' ); ?>
